WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.110
Ask people in one country
how happy they are.

2
00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:06.300
On average, the richer
ones say they are happier.

3
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.010
But as average income in the US rose after

4
00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:13.180
the Second World War, reported
happiness barely changed.

5
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:17.140
Later research found life
satisfaction does rise with income.

6
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.910
The debate continues.

7
00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.740
So can a country's
income tell you how well

8
00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:23.770
its people really live?

9
00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:26.880
In this mission, you'll compare
countries using one basket

10
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.990
of goods with two very
different price tags.

11
00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:32.870
Then you'll meet other ways
to measure how people live:

12
00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:35.860
health, schooling, even happiness.

13
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:40.050
Your mission: decide how far
income per person can take you.
